6490	{"artifactId":"HLD-ba132c185fe45860","entry":{"id":"migrated-HLD-ba132c185fe45860-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:controller","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-09-23T12:26:26.987Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"pass","summary":"review: pass","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.epic","stage":"design.epic","verdict":"pass","findings":[{"claimId":"cl1","ref":"c1","kind":"citation","severity":"LOW","premise":"The daemon registers a providers.listModels IPC handler that is currently stubbed to an offline error (offlineRpc), i.e. there is no working per-provider model list today — the entry S002 revives.","evidence":"src/daemon/index.ts:1511 read ok; grep confirms the exact line `'providers.listModels': offlineRpc('providers.listModels'),` — the offline-stubbed entry S002 revives is real and verbatim.","action":"None — citation confirmed against real source.","fixability":"auto"},{"claimId":"cl2","ref":"c1","kind":"citation","severity":"LOW","premise":"An adjacent daemon block does a live ollama tags query plus a claude static-fallback catalog via the Anthropic SDK — the forbidden direct-cloud-REST path that is NOT reusable for cloud model listing.","evidence":"src/daemon/index.ts:1282 `'claude.models': async () => {` and :1289 `const models = await client.models.list();` confirm the adjacent Anthropic-SDK cloud path exists and is the forbidden direct-REST route (correctly marked NOT reusable).","action":"None — the forbidden-path premise is confirmed; the HLD correctly excludes it.","fixability":"auto"},{"claimId":"cl3","ref":"c2","kind":"citation","severity":"LOW","premise":"The global model tiers live at models.tiers.<core|mid|cheap>.{runner,model} in the config catalog, with runner an enum over ['ollama','cli-claude','cli-codex']; the picker fills the model field and reuses this runner enum unchanged (k3).","evidence":"src/config/config-catalog.ts:96 and src/config/analyze.ts:88 both read ok; grep confirms AnalyzeShaperProviderKind and the runner union 'ollama'|'cli-claude'|'cli-codex' exist. The tier surface + reused runner enum (k3) are grounded.","action":"None — config surface + runner enum confirmed.","fixability":"auto"},{"claimId":"cl4","ref":"c3","kind":"citation","severity":"LOW","premise":"The daemon registers named JSON-RPC handlers in a map in src/daemon/index.ts served over a Unix socket, and both plugins reach the daemon only through the shared ipc-client at src/shared/ipc-client.ts — so the new list-models handler is one more read-only entry over the existing transport (no new transport/dependency).","evidence":"src/shared/ipc-client.ts:1 read ok; grep confirms createIpcClient and the config.catalog/config.show handler names — the shared client transport both plugins use is real, so the new list-models handler adds no new transport.","action":"None — shared client + handler map confirmed.","fixability":"auto"},{"claimId":"cl5","ref":"c4","kind":"citation","severity":"LOW","premise":"The daemon ships non-TS runtime resources into out/ via copy-assets.mjs, and a boot-time asset validator (docgen prior art) loads + validates shipped assets and reports a missing/malformed one — the pattern S001's curated catalog asset reuses.","evidence":"copy-assets.mjs:1 read ok and src/assets is referenced across the repo; the boot-time asset validator is docgen prior art (a real shipped epic). The asset pipeline S001 reuses exists; the specific validator wiring is S001's private internal, out of HLD scope.","action":"None — asset pipeline confirmed; validator specifics deferred to S001 LLD.","fixability":"auto"},{"claimId":"cl6","ref":"c6","kind":"citation","severity":"LOW","premise":"An existing ollama provider (src/agent/providers/ollama.ts) exposes a way to list the machine's locally-installed models, which S002's ollama branch live-queries for the local half of the list-models capability.","evidence":"src/agent/providers/ollama.ts:136 `export class OllamaProvider implements LLMProvider` confirms the existing provider; the live /api/tags query surfaces only in install scripts, so the concrete model-list method is not yet in ollama.ts. The HLD only asserts the ollama branch queries 'through the existing ollama provider' and leaves the concrete query to S002's private internal, so this is not an over-claim of an existing method.","action":"S002 LLD should specify whether it adds a tags/list method on OllamaProvider or queries the endpoint directly; no HLD change needed.","fixability":"assisted"},{"claimId":"cl7","ref":"c5","kind":"citation","severity":"LOW","premise":"VS Code model-tier config lives in native contributes.configuration (no inline live dropdown), and the JetBrains Settings page is custom Swing — so S003 uses a QuickPick command and S004 an inline combo, both dumb consumers of the S002 capability.","evidence":"vscode-plugin/package.json:1 read ok; grep confirms contributes + models.tiers in the VS Code manifest and createIpcClient shared usage. The VS Code native-config vs JetBrains-Swing asymmetry driving the QuickPick/inline-combo split is grounded.","action":"None — plugin surfaces confirmed.","fixability":"auto"},{"claimId":"cl8","kind":"ordering","severity":"LOW","premise":"The Story dependency chain is S001 → S002 → {S003, S004}: S002 depends on S001 (sc2 consumes sc1), and S003 and S004 each depend on S002 (sc2) with no edge between them, matching the approved Epic dependsOn edges.","evidence":".insrc/artifacts/DEF-ba132c185fe45860.json:1 read ok; the dependency chain S001→S002→{S003,S004} matches the approved Epic dependsOn edges (s2 dependsOn s1; s3,s4 dependsOn s2; no s3↔s4 edge), consistent with the sc1→sc2 ownership.","action":"None — ordering matches the approved DEF.","fixability":"auto"},{"claimId":"cl9","kind":"closed-union","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each shared contract has exactly one owner Story (sc1 owned by s1, sc2 owned by s2) and every Story appears in exactly one rollout phase (Phase A={s1,s2}, Phase B={s3,s4}).","evidence":".insrc/artifacts/DEF-ba132c185fe45860.json:1 read ok; each shared contract has exactly one owner (sc1→s1, sc2→s2) and every Story sits in exactly one rollout phase (A={s1,s2}, B={s3,s4}) — internally consistent, no orphan.","action":"None — contract ownership + phase coverage consistent.","fixability":"auto"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":9},"reviewedAt":"2026-09-23T12:26:26.987Z","model":"client"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
